<p style="text-align: left;"><span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><a title="Link to Health Meta Major" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/academics/metamajors/meta_healthandsafety.php"><img style="float: right;" src="https://www.ltcc.edu/_resources/images/ltcc_images/academics/metamajor_icons/health-public-safety-white-back.jpg" alt="Health Meta Major Icon" width="240" height="260" /></a></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The Physical Education and Health program at Lake Tahoe Community College is designed to provide each student with a variety of activity courses that focus on individual assessment and improvement. Currently, we offer an AA-T in Kinesiology and an AS-T in Nutrition. Academic offerings include activity courses, health, nutrition, first aid, and the sciences. These programs fully utilize outdoor facilities such as local ski areas, golf courses, Lake Tahoe itself, and the Sierra Nevada mountains.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
